WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.977 --> 00:00:09.020
Subtitle created by <font color="#ffff00">- Aorion -</font>
"The Peanuts Movie (2015)" ^ ( Run time 01:28:06 )

2
00:01:10.916 --> 00:01:12.367
Oww.

3
00:01:17.154 --> 00:01:20.493
THE
PEANUTS
MOVIE

4
00:01:24.139 --> 00:01:26.485
- Hey!
- Hey!

5
00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:41.454
Ah.
Beethoven.

6
00:01:41.479 --> 00:01:44.839
Linus.
Time to get up.

7
00:01:44.864 --> 00:01:47.512
You don't want
to be late for school.

8
00:01:47.537 --> 00:01:49.205
- Get up!
- Uh?

9
00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:51.397
Huh!
My blanket!

10
00:01:53.737 --> 00:01:55.244
Hello?

11
00:01:55.362 --> 00:01:56.769
Snow day?

12
00:01:56.794 --> 00:01:58.393
Snow day!

13
00:01:58.418 --> 00:01:59.646
Hello?

14
00:01:59.671 --> 00:02:01.693
No school today!

15
00:02:01.718 --> 00:02:03.844
Dreams do come true!

16
00:02:03.869 --> 00:02:06.398
- Woo hoo! No school.
- Yay!

17
00:02:09.193 --> 00:02:10.306
Woo hoo!

18
00:02:10.331 --> 00:02:12.751
Franklin and Peppermint Patty
are on my team.

19
00:02:12.776 --> 00:02:14.886
- I got my hockey stick.
- I got my skates.

20
00:02:14.911 --> 00:02:16.094
Who has the pugs?

21
00:02:16.119 --> 00:02:17.772
Looking sharp today, Pig-Pen.

22
00:02:17.797 --> 00:02:19.409
- Sorry, I'm late.
- Eww.

23
00:02:19.434 --> 00:02:20.943
What's taking him so long?

24
00:02:20.968 --> 00:02:23.073
- Come on, Charlie Brown!
- Come on, Charlie Brown!

25
00:02:23.098 --> 00:02:25.434
Uh, no.
Not quite.

26
00:02:25.459 --> 00:02:27.121
That's the one!

27
00:02:36.304 --> 00:02:37.818
I got my kite.

28
00:02:37.843 --> 00:02:40.024
Today's the day.
I can feel it.

29
00:02:40.049 --> 00:02:42.865
- A kite, today?
- In the middle of winter?

30
00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:46.551
- Come on, guys.
- Only Charlie Brown.

31
00:02:47.291 --> 00:02:49.720
A new kite.
A perfect breeze.

32
00:02:49.745 --> 00:02:51.594
It all feels just right.

33
00:02:51.619 --> 00:02:54.322
Now that the kite eating tree
is sleeping for the winter,

34
00:02:54.347 --> 00:02:56.821
we have nothing to fear.

35
00:02:58.582 --> 00:03:00.421
Lift off!

36
00:03:03.629 --> 00:03:04.899
Oh.

37
00:03:07.319 --> 00:03:09.198
Wait a minute.
It's in the air.

38
00:03:09.223 --> 00:03:10.350
It's flying.

39
00:03:10.375 --> 00:03:12.243
Hey, guys.
Look!

40
00:03:12.268 --> 00:03:14.113
Look, I did it!

41
00:03:20.729 --> 00:03:23.435
Hey, Charlie Brown.
Still no luck, huh?

42
00:03:23.467 --> 00:03:24.690
- Ow!
- Remember,

43
00:03:24.715 --> 00:03:27.318
It's the courage to
continue that counts!

44
00:03:27.343 --> 00:03:29.905
- Hey!
- Runaway kite.

45
00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:31.597
- Ahh!
- Sorry.

46
00:03:34.418 --> 00:03:36.802
Whoa.
No brakes.

47
00:03:36.827 --> 00:03:39.869
And now,
for my famous Triple Axel.

48
00:03:39.894 --> 00:03:42.127
Prepare to be amazed.

49
00:03:42.152 --> 00:03:43.233
Whooaa.

50
00:03:43.258 --> 00:03:46.267
- Ooo, a quadruple.
- Bravo.

51
00:03:50.321 --> 00:03:53.630
Ugh.
Stupid kite eating tree.

52
00:03:54.602 --> 00:03:55.955
Oh.

53
00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:57.900
Good grief.

54
00:03:58.062 --> 00:03:59.675
You blockhead!

55
00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:01.410
I should have known.

56
00:04:01.435 --> 00:04:04.201
What kind of a person
tries to fly a kite

57
00:04:04.226 --> 00:04:06.257
in the middle of winter?

58
00:04:06.282 --> 00:04:08.286
Don't you ever know
when to give up?

59
00:04:08.311 --> 00:04:11.253
You will never
get that kite to fly.

60
00:04:11.278 --> 00:04:15.666
Why?
Because you're Charlie Brown.

61
00:04:19.608 --> 00:04:21.700
Oh.
Thanks, Linus.

62
00:04:21.725 --> 00:04:23.082
Listen, Charlie Brown.

63
00:04:23.107 --> 00:04:25.172
Ignore what my sister, Lucy, says

64
00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:27.671
has enabled me to
make it this far in life.

65
00:04:27.696 --> 00:04:30.883
What would I do without
a good friend like you.

66
00:04:31.481 --> 00:04:33.507
Whoooaa!

67
00:04:35.899 --> 00:04:38.021
Ah.
My Sweet Babboo!

68
00:04:38.046 --> 00:04:39.458
Augh.

69
00:04:39.834 --> 00:04:42.332
Isn't he the cutest thing?

70
00:04:42.357 --> 00:04:44.584
- Yee-haw!
- Careful, sir.

71
00:04:44.609 --> 00:04:46.170
- Whoa!
- Ah!

72
00:04:47.473 --> 00:04:48.994
- Ha-ha.
- Huh?

73
00:04:49.019 --> 00:04:50.823
Mm.
Whoa.

74
00:04:51.019 --> 00:04:52.931
Watch the curls.

75
00:04:52.956 --> 00:04:54.502
Hmm.

76
00:05:02.639 --> 00:05:04.717
- Woo hoo!
- Heh-heh!

77
00:05:19.856 --> 00:05:21.566
I don't care what Lucy says.

78
00:05:21.599 --> 00:05:24.325
I may have had troubles
in the past flying a kite,

79
00:05:24.350 --> 00:05:26.604
and I may have never
won a baseball game,

80
00:05:26.629 --> 00:05:29.488
but it's not for
the lack of trying.

81
00:05:29.528 --> 00:05:31.941
My pitching has to improve
if I come out here

82
00:05:31.966 --> 00:05:34.912
to my trusty mound everyday.

83
00:05:37.782 --> 00:05:41.014
Charlie Brown is not a quitter.

84
00:05:46.838 --> 00:05:48.288
Play ball!

85
00:05:50.247 --> 00:05:52.502
Bottom of the 9th,
two outs.

86
00:05:52.527 --> 00:05:55.611
A strike out here would make
the pitcher an instant hero.

87
00:05:55.636 --> 00:05:56.664
Yay!

88
00:05:56.689 --> 00:05:57.688
- Yay!
- Yay!

89
00:05:57.713 --> 00:06:01.446
It all comes down
to this one pitch.

90
00:06:11.729 --> 00:06:14.238
Let's see if you can
handle my fast ball.

91
00:06:14.263 --> 00:06:15.784
Old number one.

92
00:06:15.809 --> 00:06:18.906
The heera.
The brown bullet.

93
00:06:23.305 --> 00:06:25.508
Oh...

94
00:06:25.885 --> 00:06:28.267
Hahaha!

95
00:06:44.386 --> 00:06:47.487
It's going to be
a long winter.

96
00:06:49.561 --> 00:06:50.809
Huh?

97
00:06:55.372 --> 00:06:57.650
Someone's moving in
across the street from me?

98
00:06:57.675 --> 00:06:59.597
Hey, gang, look.
There's a new kid moving in!

99
00:06:59.622 --> 00:07:01.745
Big brother, pull yourself together.

100
00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:03.472
Come on, Charlie Brown.

101
00:07:03.497 --> 00:07:05.013
- Get out of the way.
- Ow.

102
00:07:05.038 --> 00:07:07.716
Hey, guys, what do you see?
Who is it?

103
00:07:07.741 --> 00:07:11.010
Oh, I think I see a piano.
I hope he loves Beethoven.

104
00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:12.597
Beethoven Schmeetoven.

105
00:07:12.622 --> 00:07:15.971
Maybe he will appreciate
my natural beauty.

106
00:07:15.996 --> 00:07:17.267
Who cares about that.

107
00:07:17.292 --> 00:07:19.444
As long as he's a better
goalie than Marcie.

108
00:07:19.469 --> 00:07:22.532
- You're hurting me, sir.
- I'm sorry, but it's true.

109
00:07:22.557 --> 00:07:24.522
No, you're pulling on my hair.

110
00:07:24.547 --> 00:07:27.353
I just hope he'll have an open mind
about The Great Pumpkin.

111
00:07:27.378 --> 00:07:29.259
I think they have a toaster!

112
00:07:29.284 --> 00:07:32.523
 I just hope this new kid
has never heard of me.

113
00:07:32.617 --> 00:07:36.023
He would know nothing
of my past imperfections.

114
00:07:36.882 --> 00:07:41.237
It's not often you get the opportunity
to start over with a clean slate.

115
00:07:41.262 --> 00:07:43.523
This time, things will be different.

116
00:07:43.548 --> 00:07:45.108
Whooa!

117
00:07:51.458 --> 00:07:53.251
- He did it!
- He did it!
- Huh?

118
00:08:02.805 --> 00:08:07.428
Snoopy, why is it that everything
I try turns out wrong?

119
00:08:07.453 --> 00:08:10.706
Sometimes, I wonder
if the kids really like me.

120
00:08:10.803 --> 00:08:13.715
Maybe that new kid will
see me for who I really am,

121
00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:14.797
like you.

122
00:08:14.822 --> 00:08:18.097
A dog doesn't try to
give advice, or judge you;

123
00:08:18.122 --> 00:08:20.573
they just love you
for who you are.

124
00:08:20.598 --> 00:08:24.315
It's nice to have someone who
will just sit and listen to you.

125
00:08:24.340 --> 00:08:25.956
Zzz  Zzz.

126
00:08:25.981 --> 00:08:28.486
Zzz Zzz z.
Zzzz.

127
00:08:28.511 --> 00:08:31.324
(Sigh)
Man's best friend.

128
00:08:33.069 --> 00:08:34.872
You can't come to school, Snoopy.

129
00:08:34.897 --> 00:08:37.518
Now, be a good dog
and go home.

130
00:08:49.295 --> 00:08:51.488
No dogs allowed.

131
00:08:56.698 --> 00:08:59.723
- I think I saw the new kid.
- Did you see that new truck arrive?

132
00:08:59.748 --> 00:09:01.859
Who do you suppose it would be?

133
00:09:01.884 --> 00:09:03.915
The new kid is coming.

134
00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:05.797
- Oh.
- That's not the new kid.

135
00:09:05.822 --> 00:09:07.694
Hey, Charlie Brown.

136
00:09:10.859 --> 00:09:13.076
Good morning, Linus.
What do you have there?

137
00:09:13.101 --> 00:09:15.211
It's my turn for
show and tell today.

138
00:09:15.236 --> 00:09:18.435
This is the same plane flown
by Manfred Von Richthofen.

139
00:09:18.460 --> 00:09:20.154
- Who?
- The Red Baron.

140
00:09:20.179 --> 00:09:22.982
The most famous aviator
during the great war.

141
00:09:23.007 --> 00:09:25.149
It's not real, is it?

142
00:09:30.212 --> 00:09:33.393
Ah!
My naturally curly hair!

143
00:09:37.517 --> 00:09:39.728
- Duck, Linus.
- Whoa!

144
00:09:40.088 --> 00:09:41.322
Yikes !

145
00:09:45.039 --> 00:09:47.418
- Yes, Miss Othmar.
- Yes, Miss Othmar.

146
00:09:48.605 --> 00:09:49.853
Ew.

147
00:09:50.388 --> 00:09:51.812
Sir?

148
00:09:52.435 --> 00:09:53.902
Sir.

149
00:09:54.146 --> 00:09:55.495
Sir!

150
00:09:55.520 --> 00:09:57.245
Two!
No, three!

151
00:09:57.270 --> 00:10:01.359
- Was I close?
- Class hasn't started yet, sir.

152
00:10:01.904 --> 00:10:02.596
Huh?

153
00:10:02.621 --> 00:10:06.084
What? The new kid
is joining our class.

154
00:10:11.086 --> 00:10:13.149
She doesn't look
like a goalie to me.

155
00:10:13.174 --> 00:10:14.980
Wow.
She is pretty.

156
00:10:15.005 --> 00:10:17.627
She's not that pretty.

157
00:10:20.421 --> 00:10:22.848
Mmm, Linus.

158
00:10:22.875 --> 00:10:25.578
Huh!
She looked at me.

159
00:10:33.415 --> 00:10:34.415
- Aww!
- Aww!

160
00:10:34.441 --> 00:10:37.358
- Not the yearly standardized test again!
- Not the yearly standardized test again!

161
00:10:37.383 --> 00:10:42.305
Ma'am, will this test, accurately reflect
the knowledge we have gained here?

162
00:10:42.551 --> 00:10:45.858
Is it fair, we at this young age...

163
00:10:46.533 --> 00:10:48.296
Yes, ma'am.

164
00:10:52.529 --> 00:10:54.957
(Sigh) Thanks.

165
00:10:54.982 --> 00:10:58.641
Question 1:
If you had 6 red tomatoes and...

166
00:10:58.666 --> 00:11:01.334
Uh.
Red.

167
00:11:12.392 --> 00:11:14.257
Come on, focus.

168
00:11:14.282 --> 00:11:16.848
First impressions are everything.

169
00:11:39.615 --> 00:11:41.810
AUGH !

170
00:11:42.656 --> 00:11:45.005
No dogs!

171
00:11:59.100 --> 00:12:00.505
Already done?

172
00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:02.989
She must be smart.

173
00:12:12.912 --> 00:12:16.388
Huh?
It's got teeth marks.

174
00:12:17.427 --> 00:12:19.710
She nibbles on
her pencil like I do.

175
00:12:19.735 --> 00:12:22.110
We have something in common!

176
00:12:22.135 --> 00:12:24.377
Huh!
One minute left?

177
00:12:31.699 --> 00:12:33.852
Out of my way, Chuck.

178
00:12:35.218 --> 00:12:37.835
Write our names?
Yes, ma'am.

179
00:12:40.105 --> 00:12:42.984
Chuck, are you trying
to hold my hand?

180
00:12:43.009 --> 00:12:44.452
You sly dog.

181
00:12:44.477 --> 00:12:45.684
- Ooo.
- Ooo.

182
00:12:45.709 --> 00:12:47.427
Huh! Ah!
Um.

183
00:12:47.452 --> 00:12:50.877
Hi, I'm Brown Charlie.
I mean, Barney Clown.

184
00:12:50.902 --> 00:12:52.513
I... I mean...

185
00:12:57.509 --> 00:13:00.256
What... What...
What are you in for?

186
00:13:00.281 --> 00:13:03.248
Have you ever had that feeling
 when you can't stop smiling?

187
00:13:03.273 --> 00:13:04.505
Huh?

188
00:13:04.752 --> 00:13:07.489
Your heart pounds inside your chest.

189
00:13:07.514 --> 00:13:10.392
You try to stand,
but your knees become weak.

190
00:13:10.417 --> 00:13:11.437
Huh!

191
00:13:11.467 --> 00:13:14.860
And then that Little
Red-Haired Girl glances at you

192
00:13:14.885 --> 00:13:15.698
Whoa.

193
00:13:15.723 --> 00:13:20.315
and all of life's possibilities
become so clear.

194
00:13:20.361 --> 00:13:22.170
And then you realize...

195
00:13:22.195 --> 00:13:23.299
WHOA!

196
00:13:23.324 --> 00:13:26.893
she has no idea you're alive.

197
00:13:26.943 --> 00:13:28.328
Why am I here?

198
00:13:28.368 --> 00:13:33.297
(Sigh) Because I just came down
with a serious case of inadequacy.

199
00:13:42.332 --> 00:13:44.017
Hmm.

200
00:13:46.238 --> 00:13:47.345
Huh?

201
00:13:49.061 --> 00:13:51.000
Whoa. Whoa.
Whoa. Whoa!

202
00:13:57.738 --> 00:13:59.504
AAUGH !

203
00:14:13.222 --> 00:14:15.187
OOO.

204
00:14:21.931 --> 00:14:22.991
Ow...

205
00:14:23.016 --> 00:14:24.240
Yikes !

206
00:14:27.407 --> 00:14:29.475
See you tomorrow.

207
00:14:31.045 --> 00:14:33.100
Hey, that's my seat!

208
00:14:33.550 --> 00:14:35.563
Huh, here she comes.

209
00:14:35.608 --> 00:14:38.558
This is my chance to
make a good impression.

210
00:14:42.594 --> 00:14:43.921
Maybe tomorrow.

211
00:14:43.946 --> 00:14:45.463
Ow!

212
00:15:18.894 --> 00:15:20.189
Yikes.

213
00:15:20.214 --> 00:15:21.698
- Augh!
- Augh!

214
00:15:24.859 --> 00:15:28.032
It was a dark
and stormy night

215
00:15:28.232 --> 00:15:29.842
Hmm.

216
00:15:30.874 --> 00:15:33.134
High above the French countryside,

217
00:15:33.159 --> 00:15:37.287
the World War I Flying Ace
had never been so close...

218
00:15:37.312 --> 00:15:39.200
- Ha ha ha!
- to his life long enemy,

219
00:15:39.225 --> 00:15:42.127
the infamous Red Baron.

220
00:16:30.068 --> 00:16:31.309
Huh?

221
00:16:51.197 --> 00:16:52.916
Shhhh.

222
00:17:04.718 --> 00:17:07.728
The key, is keeping a low profile.

223
00:17:07.753 --> 00:17:10.607
For now, we just keep our distance.

224
00:17:14.188 --> 00:17:16.323
Ahh!
Snoopy!

225
00:17:16.775 --> 00:17:18.185
No!

226
00:17:21.234 --> 00:17:24.291
Woo.
That was a close one.

227
00:17:31.960 --> 00:17:35.455
If I could only work up
the nerve to go over there, I...

228
00:17:35.480 --> 00:17:37.018
What are you looking at, big brother?

229
00:17:37.043 --> 00:17:38.661
Whooa!
Are you crazy?

230
00:17:38.686 --> 00:17:40.025
Huh?

231
00:17:40.287 --> 00:17:42.028
Ohhhh.

232
00:17:42.053 --> 00:17:44.420
You're in love.

233
00:17:44.726 --> 00:17:46.098
(Sigh)

234
00:17:46.328 --> 00:17:48.872
Ha ha ha!
Hmm.

235
00:17:54.647 --> 00:17:56.200
Chapter 1

236
00:17:56.225 --> 00:17:59.583
It was the greatest
love story ever told...

237
00:18:01.723 --> 00:18:03.429
♥ Fifi ♥

238
00:18:14.489 --> 00:18:15.592
Huh?

239
00:18:32.875 --> 00:18:34.710
Her name was Fifi.

240
00:18:34.735 --> 00:18:35.615
Wow!

241
00:18:35.640 --> 00:18:39.842
She was the most beautiful thing
he had ever seen.

242
00:19:48.701 --> 00:19:50.304
BLEH !

243
00:19:51.011 --> 00:19:52.408
YUCK!

244
00:20:09.431 --> 00:20:13.038
I can't believe I'm about to talk
to the Little Red-Haired Girl.

245
00:20:13.063 --> 00:20:16.729
It's moments like this when
you need your faithful friend.

246
00:20:24.322 --> 00:20:28.993
Yup. If there's one person you want
by your side at a moment like this,

247
00:20:29.018 --> 00:20:31.302
it's your loyal dog.

248
00:20:32.538 --> 00:20:36.954
Uhh...
Uhhh...

249
00:20:39.684 --> 00:20:41.106
(Sigh)

250
00:20:41.596 --> 00:20:42.997
(Sigh)

251
00:20:44.556 --> 00:20:46.179
AAUGH !

252
00:20:47.033 --> 00:20:48.458
Hello?

253
00:20:48.483 --> 00:20:49.901
Hello ??

254
00:20:49.926 --> 00:20:51.134
Hm.

255
00:20:52.896 --> 00:20:54.411
She said, "Hello" !

256
00:20:54.436 --> 00:20:55.762
Aww.

257
00:21:00.130 --> 00:21:02.172
<font color="#f9ad68">PSYCHIATRIC
HELP  5 cents</font>

258
00:21:02.197 --> 00:21:03.824
Charlie Brown.

259
00:21:03.849 --> 00:21:06.495
What brings you out here
so late in the day?

260
00:21:06.520 --> 00:21:09.661
(Sigh)
I need your advise on girls, Lucy.

261
00:21:09.686 --> 00:21:11.335
You're a girl, right?

262
00:21:11.360 --> 00:21:14.075
Let's just say there is this girl
I like to impress.

263
00:21:14.100 --> 00:21:16.707
But she's something
and I'm nothing.

264
00:21:16.742 --> 00:21:18.744
If I were something
and she was nothing,

265
00:21:18.769 --> 00:21:20.162
I could talk to her.

266
00:21:20.187 --> 00:21:22.071
Or she was nothing
and I was nothing,

267
00:21:22.096 --> 00:21:23.336
I could talk to her.

268
00:21:23.361 --> 00:21:26.523
But she's something
and I'm nothing.

269
00:21:26.548 --> 00:21:28.341
So, I just can't just talk to her.

270
00:21:28.366 --> 00:21:32.465
You're being ridiculous, Charlie Brown.
Why, you have much to offer.

271
00:21:32.490 --> 00:21:35.828
She has a pretty face
and pretty faces make me nervous.

272
00:21:35.853 --> 00:21:38.600
Pretty face?
PRETTY FACE?

273
00:21:38.625 --> 00:21:40.130
I HAVE A PRETTY FACE!

274
00:21:40.155 --> 00:21:42.373
HOW COME MY FACE
DOESN'T MAKE YOU NERVOUS?

275
00:21:42.398 --> 00:21:45.826
HOW COME YOU CAN TALK TO ME,
CHARLIE BROWN ?

276
00:21:48.677 --> 00:21:52.570
I just need to know the secret
to winning her heart.

277
00:21:52.595 --> 00:21:55.292
Look into this mirror, Charlie Brown.

278
00:21:55.317 --> 00:22:00.114
This is the face of failure.
A classic failure face.

279
00:22:00.150 --> 00:22:02.484
Do you think girls like failures,
Charlie Brown?

280
00:22:02.519 --> 00:22:03.659
Well, no.

281
00:22:03.694 --> 00:22:06.106
Girls want someone with proven success.

282
00:22:06.141 --> 00:22:07.884
Have you won any awards?

283
00:22:07.909 --> 00:22:11.526
Like a Congressional Medal of Honor,
or a Nobel Peace Prize?

284
00:22:11.551 --> 00:22:12.489
Uh...

285
00:22:12.514 --> 00:22:14.224
What are your real estate holdings?

286
00:22:14.253 --> 00:22:17.091
- Do you have a diversified portfolio?
- Huh?

287
00:22:17.116 --> 00:22:20.203
Let me let you in on a
little secret, Charlie Brown.

288
00:22:20.263 --> 00:22:24.853
 If you really want to impress girls,
 you need to show them you're a winner.

289
00:22:24.878 --> 00:22:27.111
A winner?
Me?

290
00:22:27.136 --> 00:22:29.600
Lucy, you may be on to something!

291
00:22:29.625 --> 00:22:31.944
Of course, when I say "you",

292
00:22:31.969 --> 00:22:34.817
you know I don't mean "you personally".

293
00:22:37.300 --> 00:22:39.766
That would be 5 cents, please.

294
00:22:42.915 --> 00:22:44.001
Ahhh.

295
00:22:44.026 --> 00:22:48.340
Nickels. Nickels. Nickels.
What a beautiful sound.

296
00:22:48.369 --> 00:22:51.971
Congratulations, you're now on
your way to becoming a winner.

297
00:22:51.996 --> 00:22:55.844
Step 1: Forget everything you
ever knew about yourself.

298
00:22:55.869 --> 00:22:58.254
Hmm.
Okay.

299
00:22:58.279 --> 00:23:01.456
Step 2: Project confidence!

300
00:23:01.481 --> 00:23:03.187
Don't slouch!

301
00:23:05.796 --> 00:23:09.171
Maintain eye contact at all times.

302
00:23:22.479 --> 00:23:25.072
Ha ha!
Ha ha ha.

303
00:23:25.097 --> 00:23:27.558
- Huh!
- Yee-haw!

304
00:23:29.241 --> 00:23:33.084
Giddy-up, little pony.
Yee-haw!

305
00:23:33.109 --> 00:23:34.219
What're you doing?

306
00:23:34.244 --> 00:23:37.944
I'm going to be a rodeo star
in the big talent show.

307
00:23:37.969 --> 00:23:40.258
Why, when I win
that first prize ribbon

308
00:23:40.283 --> 00:23:42.958
there will be no one who hasn't
heard the name, Sally Brown,

309
00:23:42.983 --> 00:23:45.829
and her trusty horse, Broomstick.

310
00:23:45.854 --> 00:23:49.749
Win the talent show.
Now, that's a great idea.

311
00:23:49.774 --> 00:23:53.074
This is just what
Lucy was talking about.

312
00:24:03.429 --> 00:24:04.806
Ha ha.

313
00:24:09.418 --> 00:24:11.105
Ta-da!

314
00:24:11.569 --> 00:24:12.694
Yikes!

315
00:24:33.984 --> 00:24:35.815
We're ready.

316
00:24:51.319 --> 00:24:53.376
- Whoa. Look at that.
- Whoa. It's Charlie Brown.

317
00:24:53.401 --> 00:24:55.263
- Is that Charlie Brown?
- That's impressive.

318
00:24:55.308 --> 00:24:56.431
Ooo.

319
00:24:56.482 --> 00:24:58.641
You're the next Houdini, Charlie Brown.

320
00:24:58.666 --> 00:25:00.033
Whoa.

321
00:25:05.563 --> 00:25:07.511
Huh.
She's here.

322
00:25:07.536 --> 00:25:09.416
I've a really good
feeling that tonight

323
00:25:09.451 --> 00:25:11.984
she will see the 
new Charlie Brown.

324
00:25:12.009 --> 00:25:13.669
Charlie Brown?

325
00:25:13.694 --> 00:25:17.103
As your psychiatrist,
I'm surprise to see you here.

326
00:25:17.133 --> 00:25:21.512
A person with all your insecurities
normally wouldn't enter a talent show.

327
00:25:21.552 --> 00:25:22.605
I'm...

328
00:25:22.630 --> 00:25:24.513
Ha! Ha ha!
Ha ha ha...

329
00:25:24.538 --> 00:25:27.111
I oughta slug you.

330
00:25:27.319 --> 00:25:29.995
Ugh!
I've been kissed by a dog!

331
00:25:30.020 --> 00:25:32.412
I have dog germs!
Get hot water!

332
00:25:32.437 --> 00:25:35.208
Get some disinfected!
Get some Iodine!

333
00:25:35.233 --> 00:25:38.825
Let's keep this thing moving!
Time's a wastin.

334
00:25:41.401 --> 00:25:42.349
- Heeyah!
- Ugh.

335
00:25:42.373 --> 00:25:44.270
- Hiyah! Hi!
- Ow!

336
00:25:44.295 --> 00:25:47.968
Thank you.
Break a leg, Chuck.

337
00:25:49.239 --> 00:25:52.480
Treat you assistant kindly, Charles.

338
00:25:52.505 --> 00:25:54.298
Okay, Sally.
We're running behind,

339
00:25:54.323 --> 00:25:56.845
so, gallop, don't trot.

340
00:25:58.921 --> 00:26:01.779
Save the applause for the end, everyone.

341
00:26:02.531 --> 00:26:05.921
If you like this,
wait for the encore.

342
00:26:08.180 --> 00:26:12.217
Ugh. Your sister is
really dying out there.

343
00:26:12.242 --> 00:26:15.388
Hey.
That's not a real horse.

344
00:26:19.500 --> 00:26:22.618
Sorry, Charlie Brown,
this has gone on long enough.

345
00:26:22.643 --> 00:26:23.787
Drop the curtain!

346
00:26:23.812 --> 00:26:26.323
Don't do that. She said
she has a big finish.

347
00:26:26.348 --> 00:26:30.608
Well, it's either your act or her's,
we can't hold on forever.

348
00:26:39.020 --> 00:26:40.703
Hey!

349
00:26:40.728 --> 00:26:43.457
- Huh?
- Change of plan, Snoopy.

350
00:26:44.012 --> 00:26:45.492
Wow.

351
00:26:47.487 --> 00:26:49.561
Moo!

352
00:26:49.586 --> 00:26:52.343
Mooooo!

353
00:26:53.646 --> 00:26:55.728
Big brother?

354
00:26:55.971 --> 00:26:57.289
Rope me!

355
00:26:57.314 --> 00:27:00.451
- Moo!
- That's not a real cow.

356
00:27:05.258 --> 00:27:07.617
I'm gonna get you.

357
00:27:07.848 --> 00:27:09.217
Huh?

358
00:27:09.461 --> 00:27:11.072
Huh!
Whooa !

359
00:27:11.097 --> 00:27:12.214
Yoo hoo!

360
00:27:12.239 --> 00:27:13.610
Ahh!

361
00:27:15.446 --> 00:27:16.861
Yah!

362
00:27:16.886 --> 00:27:19.195
- Huh?
- Hi yah!

363
00:27:19.702 --> 00:27:21.586
- Sorry, sir.
- Good one!

364
00:27:21.611 --> 00:27:23.162
Oh, Schroeder.

365
00:27:23.187 --> 00:27:24.535
Huh!

366
00:27:29.012 --> 00:27:33.175
You can run, little doggy,
but, you can't hide.

367
00:27:36.831 --> 00:27:39.889
This is going great.
Yee haw!

368
00:27:40.690 --> 00:27:43.545
My name is Calamity Sally,

369
00:27:43.570 --> 00:27:48.720
the best bronco-busting,
lasso-roping cowgirl in this here town.

370
00:27:54.042 --> 00:27:56.113
Thanks, big brother.

371
00:27:59.267 --> 00:28:00.943
Whoooaa.

372
00:28:03.418 --> 00:28:04.855
Moo?

373
00:28:05.269 --> 00:28:08.692
Well, no body reads
the school paper anyhow.

374
00:28:09.330 --> 00:28:10.629
Huh!

375
00:28:11.817 --> 00:28:13.589
Look on the bright side, Charlie Brown.

376
00:28:13.614 --> 00:28:16.965
They say there's no such
thing as bad publicity.

377
00:28:16.995 --> 00:28:18.152
You're right, Linus.

378
00:28:18.177 --> 00:28:20.918
She definitely knows
who I am now.

379
00:28:20.943 --> 00:28:22.765
(Peanut butter again.)
Huh!

380
00:28:24.006 --> 00:28:26.884
You know, Charlie Brown,
if you like her so much,

381
00:28:26.909 --> 00:28:29.905
why not just walk up to her
and introduce yourself?

382
00:28:29.930 --> 00:28:33.308
After the complete fool
I made out of myself last night?

383
00:28:33.333 --> 00:28:36.914
Yeah, and why don't I
just fly to the moon?

384
00:28:39.838 --> 00:28:43.190
Oh, brother,
she's talking to them?

385
00:28:43.215 --> 00:28:46.059
So much for a fresh start.

386
00:28:46.084 --> 00:28:48.249
Time is running out!

387
00:28:48.967 --> 00:28:53.290
Number 6: Tell yourself,
" I am worthy, I can do this!

388
00:28:53.315 --> 00:28:55.539
I have what it takes."

389
00:28:55.625 --> 00:28:56.924
Hello?

390
00:28:56.949 --> 00:28:58.152
Huh!

391
00:28:58.517 --> 00:29:01.530
You girlfriend's on the phone.

392
00:29:01.555 --> 00:29:02.833
Huh!

393
00:29:04.635 --> 00:29:05.797
- Hello.
- Hey, Chuck!

394
00:29:05.822 --> 00:29:08.021
This is Peppermint Patty.
How've you been?

395
00:29:08.046 --> 00:29:09.166
- Well, I...
- Listen.

396
00:29:09.191 --> 00:29:11.276
I've some great news
for you, Chuck.

397
00:29:11.306 --> 00:29:13.028
The Winter Dance
is in a few weeks.

398
00:29:13.068 --> 00:29:15.520
- and I'm saving a dance for you.
- Huh?

399
00:29:15.545 --> 00:29:18.848
Anyway, Marcie put me in charge
of the refreshment committee.

400
00:29:18.873 --> 00:29:22.502
I took it upon myself and signed
you up to make the cupcakes.

401
00:29:22.527 --> 00:29:25.115
You did what?
I can't cook cupcakes.

402
00:29:25.140 --> 00:29:27.608
The only thing I do know
how to make is toast.

403
00:29:27.633 --> 00:29:30.759
Besides, why would I even want
to go to the Winter Dance.

404
00:29:30.784 --> 00:29:31.943
Toast and cupcakes.

405
00:29:31.968 --> 00:29:34.280
That sounds good, Chuck.
See you there!

406
00:29:34.305 --> 00:29:36.174
Hold on!
I said...

407
00:29:36.199 --> 00:29:38.747
Hello.
Hello?

408
00:29:40.508 --> 00:29:42.926
Ugh.
Rats.

409
00:29:48.598 --> 00:29:51.949
Ugh.
(Sigh)

410
00:30:14.258 --> 00:30:16.811
Hey!
What's going on?

411
00:30:17.692 --> 00:30:21.038
Turn it down!
Turn it down in there!

412
00:30:23.447 --> 00:30:24.718
Huh?

413
00:30:24.971 --> 00:30:27.033
She likes to dance.

414
00:30:27.058 --> 00:30:28.369
Ugh!

415
00:30:36.459 --> 00:30:40.375
♪ Bamboleo bambolea ♪

416
00:30:40.496 --> 00:30:46.898
♪ Porque mi vida yo la prefiero
vivir asi ♪

417
00:30:48.451 --> 00:30:50.029
Mmm.

418
00:30:57.160 --> 00:30:58.544
Ugh.

419
00:31:15.857 --> 00:31:19.369
One. Two.
Three. Four.

420
00:31:19.394 --> 00:31:22.763
One. Two.
Three. Four.

421
00:31:22.850 --> 00:31:27.538
One. Two.
Three. Four.

422
00:31:27.615 --> 00:31:31.895
One. Two.
Three. Four.

423
00:31:31.920 --> 00:31:33.150
Huh!

424
00:31:36.636 --> 00:31:40.055
- I could really use a dance partner.
- Good luck with that!

425
00:31:40.080 --> 00:31:42.647
One. Two.
Three. Four.

426
00:31:42.672 --> 00:31:45.286
Okay, Snoopy.
I got the basics down.

427
00:31:45.311 --> 00:31:48.797
But, if I'm gonna win,
I need to step it up.

428
00:31:51.099 --> 00:31:55.121
One. Two.
Three. Four.

429
00:31:55.146 --> 00:31:57.492
I can see it now...

430
00:32:04.289 --> 00:32:06.485
We have our winners!

431
00:32:06.516 --> 00:32:08.533
Let us applaud them, as they begin

432
00:32:08.558 --> 00:32:12.438
the traditional dance of the champions.

433
00:32:17.699 --> 00:32:18.946
Huh?

434
00:32:20.781 --> 00:32:22.422
Snoopy!

435
00:32:23.114 --> 00:32:24.396
Thanks for the help.

436
00:32:24.421 --> 00:32:27.243
I left some cookies
in your dog dish.

437
00:32:27.268 --> 00:32:30.612
One. Two.
Three. Four.

438
00:32:30.834 --> 00:32:33.111
One. Two.

439
00:32:38.053 --> 00:32:39.973
<font color="#a4d1ff">[WINTER DANCE]</font>

440
00:32:41.987 --> 00:32:44.669
You know, I always wanted
to dance with Pig-Pen.

441
00:32:44.694 --> 00:32:47.064
Uh, yuck!

442
00:32:48.845 --> 00:32:53.032
Why isn't anyone dancing?
It's called a dance!

443
00:32:53.541 --> 00:32:55.263
Hey, guys.
Huh!

444
00:32:55.288 --> 00:32:57.869
- Oh, sweet babboo.
- Oh, no. Here she comes.

445
00:32:57.894 --> 00:33:00.124
Someone needs to
get this dance started.

446
00:33:00.149 --> 00:33:01.944
- No. No.
- Woo.

447
00:33:20.224 --> 00:33:24.787
These cupcakes don't look half-bad,
if I do say so myself.

448
00:33:24.812 --> 00:33:28.073
This time, I've come totally prepared.

449
00:33:28.098 --> 00:33:30.285
I couldn't have done it
without you.

450
00:33:30.310 --> 00:33:34.582
The old Charlie Brown would still be
lying in bed with a stomachache.

451
00:33:35.773 --> 00:33:37.149
Huh?

452
00:33:39.506 --> 00:33:41.347
Good grief.

453
00:33:47.114 --> 00:33:50.451
Marcie, look, everyone's here.

454
00:33:50.913 --> 00:33:53.915
Oh, let me help you
with that, Marcie.

455
00:33:53.940 --> 00:33:56.686
Such a gentleman, Charles.

456
00:33:58.530 --> 00:34:00.145
She's here.

457
00:34:00.170 --> 00:34:02.454
Best party ever!

458
00:34:02.769 --> 00:34:03.850
Huh?

459
00:34:03.874 --> 00:34:07.598
Okay, ladies, it's time for you
to show off your best moves.

460
00:34:07.623 --> 00:34:11.028
Which one of you will win the
first half of our dance competition

461
00:34:11.053 --> 00:34:12.796
and take home the trophy.

462
00:34:12.821 --> 00:34:15.036
Let them hear it!

463
00:34:15.061 --> 00:34:16.797
Nice move.

464
00:34:16.822 --> 00:34:20.622
Yay! Yay! Yay!
Yay! Yay! Yay!

465
00:34:21.480 --> 00:34:22.632
- Yay!
- Yay!

466
00:34:22.657 --> 00:34:24.258
Listen to that noise,

467
00:34:24.283 --> 00:34:27.679
I think it's safe to say
we know who our winner is!

468
00:34:27.704 --> 00:34:29.003
- She won.
- And now,

469
00:34:29.028 --> 00:34:32.954
it's the gentlemen's turn to see who
will be joining our lovely winning lady

470
00:34:32.979 --> 00:34:34.846
for the final dance of the night.

471
00:34:34.871 --> 00:34:36.146
I got to get out there.

472
00:34:36.171 --> 00:34:37.931
Are you guys ready?

473
00:34:37.956 --> 00:34:40.266
Then, here we go!

474
00:34:54.675 --> 00:34:56.228
This is it.

475
00:34:56.806 --> 00:34:59.177
It's now or never.

476
00:35:09.278 --> 00:35:10.291
Whoa!

477
00:35:10.316 --> 00:35:14.916
Check out the moves on that
funny-looking kid with a big nose!

478
00:35:15.338 --> 00:35:17.903
Yeah.
All right!

479
00:35:28.774 --> 00:35:33.768
Okay, just like you practiced.
Remember the steps.

480
00:35:33.928 --> 00:35:40.370
One. Two.
Three. Four.

481
00:35:45.915 --> 00:35:48.817
- Charlie Brown?
- All right.

482
00:35:49.471 --> 00:35:51.951
It looks like we may
have a winner here!

483
00:35:51.976 --> 00:35:53.214
It's gonna happen.

484
00:35:53.239 --> 00:35:56.410
I'm about to dance with
the Little Red-Haired Girl.

485
00:35:57.601 --> 00:35:59.248
Whoa!

486
00:35:59.779 --> 00:36:01.729
Whoa !!

487
00:36:04.051 --> 00:36:05.947
Ugh!
Let's get outta here!

488
00:36:05.972 --> 00:36:07.365
Ahh!

489
00:36:09.311 --> 00:36:11.864
- Do I know you?
- Huh?

490
00:36:13.317 --> 00:36:15.910
Wait.
It's not over yet!

491
00:36:20.911 --> 00:36:22.773
Thanks, buddy.

492
00:36:26.011 --> 00:36:27.901
I hate to say it, Snoopy.

493
00:36:27.926 --> 00:36:32.532
It seems like the harder I try,
the further away she gets.

494
00:36:45.828 --> 00:36:48.614
The Flying Ace took to the skies,

495
00:36:48.639 --> 00:36:53.115
he search endless for the girl
who has stolen his heart.

496
00:36:55.602 --> 00:36:57.294
Ha ha!

497
00:36:58.219 --> 00:36:59.805
Hi!

498
00:37:02.893 --> 00:37:04.347
Hey!

499
00:37:04.372 --> 00:37:05.604
Huh?

500
00:37:20.729 --> 00:37:22.205
Cheese!

501
00:37:28.295 --> 00:37:29.451
Oh!

502
00:37:35.299 --> 00:37:36.653
Ha ha!

503
00:38:23.921 --> 00:38:25.854
AAHHHH !

504
00:39:06.745 --> 00:39:09.464
Daydreaming will not make
her materialized, Charlie Brown.

505
00:39:09.497 --> 00:39:11.869
- She's not here.
- Daydreaming? Me?

506
00:39:11.894 --> 00:39:13.276
She'll be back on Monday.

507
00:39:13.301 --> 00:39:14.910
I heard she went back
East to take care

508
00:39:14.935 --> 00:39:16.891
of her grandmother,
who isn't feeling well.

509
00:39:16.916 --> 00:39:20.687
She seems like the kind of person
who would do that sort of thing.

510
00:39:21.101 --> 00:39:24.138
- Aww! Not another book report!
- Aww! Not another book report!

511
00:39:24.163 --> 00:39:26.059
Time to pick our partners.

512
00:39:26.084 --> 00:39:30.193
No boys! No boys!
Please.

513
00:39:30.218 --> 00:39:33.472
- Patty!
- Yes! All right!

514
00:39:33.722 --> 00:39:35.017
Nope.

515
00:39:35.239 --> 00:39:36.775
Uh-uh.

516
00:39:36.820 --> 00:39:38.250
Yes!

517
00:39:39.592 --> 00:39:41.000
Schroeder!

518
00:39:41.025 --> 00:39:45.756
There's no denying it,
it was written in the cards.

519
00:39:47.792 --> 00:39:49.320
(Sigh)

520
00:40:00.796 --> 00:40:03.778
The Little Red-Haired Girl.
My lucky day.

521
00:40:03.803 --> 00:40:07.190
This changes everything.
She will see the new me.

522
00:40:07.215 --> 00:40:09.693
And together,
we'll win the gold star!

523
00:40:09.718 --> 00:40:12.032
After that, anything is possible.

524
00:40:12.057 --> 00:40:14.289
We could be the first kids
to land on the moon.

525
00:40:14.314 --> 00:40:19.507
One small step for kids,
one giant leap for Charlie Brown.

526
00:40:19.682 --> 00:40:20.979
Huh?

527
00:40:22.469 --> 00:40:24.023
You gotta help me, Linus!

528
00:40:24.048 --> 00:40:27.544
I'm not sure I can handle being partners
with the Little Red-Haired Girl.

529
00:40:27.569 --> 00:40:29.329
I need to slow things down.

530
00:40:29.354 --> 00:40:32.040
Maybe I'm not ready
for a serious relationship.

531
00:40:32.065 --> 00:40:35.272
How will I support her?
I can't afford a mortgage.

532
00:40:35.297 --> 00:40:36.903
What if I'm put into escrow?

533
00:40:36.928 --> 00:40:40.060
Charlie Brown, you're being ridiculous.

534
00:40:40.085 --> 00:40:41.520
You're the only person I know

535
00:40:41.545 --> 00:40:45.052
who can turn a simple book report
into a lifelong commitment.

536
00:40:45.077 --> 00:40:48.328
I've never been responsible
for anything before.

537
00:40:48.353 --> 00:40:51.782
This could be the worst thing
that's ever happened to her!

538
00:40:55.011 --> 00:40:57.150
Linus, it just hit me.

539
00:40:57.175 --> 00:40:59.438
I think I know how
to become her hero!

540
00:40:59.463 --> 00:41:01.850
While she's away taking care
of her grandmother,

541
00:41:01.875 --> 00:41:04.994
I could complete the book
report for the two of us.

542
00:41:05.019 --> 00:41:06.847
That's one way to go.

543
00:41:06.872 --> 00:41:09.488
But, if you want my advice...

544
00:41:10.528 --> 00:41:13.736
They're posting the test scores!
Come on!

545
00:41:14.047 --> 00:41:16.682
Look.
Someone got a perfect score, sir.

546
00:41:16.707 --> 00:41:19.389
You would have to be a genius
to get a perfect score.

547
00:41:19.414 --> 00:41:20.935
I didn't know that
was even possible.

548
00:41:20.960 --> 00:41:22.578
- It's him.
- Here he comes.

549
00:41:22.603 --> 00:41:26.258
No one in the world has ever
gotten a hundred before.

550
00:41:29.889 --> 00:41:31.940
2. Marcie Carlin     92
3. Franklin             90

551
00:41:31.965 --> 00:41:34.863
A perfect score?
Me?

552
00:41:35.416 --> 00:41:36.639
This can't be right.

553
00:41:36.664 --> 00:41:38.051
No, Charlie Brown, look.

554
00:41:38.076 --> 00:41:40.007
You really do have
a perfect score.

555
00:41:40.032 --> 00:41:43.016
Huh. I have heard
peanut butter is brain food.

556
00:41:43.041 --> 00:41:44.766
Nice job, Chuck old boy.

557
00:41:44.791 --> 00:41:47.188
I always knew you
had it in you, Charles.

558
00:41:47.213 --> 00:41:50.151
This can't be right!
Out of my way!

559
00:41:50.176 --> 00:41:52.434
Mr. Perfect: Charlie Brown?

560
00:41:52.459 --> 00:41:54.942
It must be a typo!
I don't believe it.

561
00:41:54.967 --> 00:41:58.415
I won't believe it!
I demand a recount!

562
00:41:58.440 --> 00:42:01.754
Good afternoon, students and staff.
We have a special announcement.

563
00:42:01.779 --> 00:42:04.169
There will be an all-school assembly
on Monday morning

564
00:42:04.194 --> 00:42:07.115
to celebrate our illustrious classmate,
Charlie Brown,

565
00:42:07.140 --> 00:42:10.368
who achieved a perfect score
on the standardized test.

566
00:42:10.393 --> 00:42:13.119
Make way.
Genius coming through.

567
00:42:13.144 --> 00:42:16.129
I have a science project due next week,
can you give me you thoughts?

568
00:42:16.154 --> 00:42:17.508
Hey!
I saw him first.

569
00:42:17.533 --> 00:42:20.676
They say you're a genius.
Can you read my mind?

570
00:42:20.701 --> 00:42:23.576
- Hey, leave him alone.
- Yeah, leave him alone!

571
00:42:23.601 --> 00:42:26.853
Now, Charlie Brown,
as far as the book report goes,

572
00:42:26.878 --> 00:42:28.644
what would you suggest?

573
00:42:28.669 --> 00:42:31.913
Well, you can never go wrong
if you stick with the classics.

574
00:42:31.938 --> 00:42:33.226
A comic book?
[SPARK PLUG]

575
00:42:33.258 --> 00:42:35.181
I thought classics had
to have hard covers?

576
00:42:35.206 --> 00:42:38.542
Boy, do we feel stupid now.

577
00:42:41.739 --> 00:42:45.095
Will you look at this.
What a contemporary piece.

578
00:42:45.120 --> 00:42:47.458
Notice his use of space.

579
00:42:47.483 --> 00:42:50.207
Have you all lost your minds?

580
00:42:53.764 --> 00:42:55.270
Whoa.

581
00:42:57.465 --> 00:43:00.817
You have what is referred
to as irrational fear.

582
00:43:01.325 --> 00:43:02.406
Huh?

583
00:43:02.431 --> 00:43:04.601
Hey, kid.
What do you think you're doing?

584
00:43:04.626 --> 00:43:07.336
Following in the
footsteps of goodness.

585
00:43:07.361 --> 00:43:10.663
- Break away!
- Shoot it, Charlie Brown! Shoot it!

586
00:43:15.540 --> 00:43:17.941
Nice use of angles there, Charles.

587
00:43:17.966 --> 00:43:19.793
- All right! Charlie Brown.
- Whoa!

588
00:43:19.818 --> 00:43:21.168
Hmm.

589
00:43:21.193 --> 00:43:24.372
How is Santa ever gonna
find our house without lights?

590
00:43:24.397 --> 00:43:25.770
Hm.

591
00:43:27.474 --> 00:43:29.086
- Yay!
- Yay!

592
00:43:29.120 --> 00:43:31.497
This is where it all began.

593
00:43:31.522 --> 00:43:34.487
As a youth he passed many hours
just sitting in that chair,

594
00:43:34.512 --> 00:43:36.814
 keeping his deep thoughts to himself.

595
00:43:36.839 --> 00:43:41.235
And here we have his early kites,
used in many aerodynamic studies.

596
00:43:41.260 --> 00:43:42.299
- Whoa.
- Wow.
- Ooo.

597
00:43:42.324 --> 00:43:45.738
If we are lucky, we will see
him in his natural habitat.

598
00:43:45.763 --> 00:43:47.394
And this is his actual bed

599
00:43:47.419 --> 00:43:50.538
where he lies and ponders
life's greatest questions.

600
00:43:50.563 --> 00:43:52.272
Hey!
What are you doing?

601
00:43:52.297 --> 00:43:55.081
I'm cashing in on your celebrity.

602
00:43:55.106 --> 00:43:56.639
BOY GENIUS!
PERFECT SCORE!

603
00:43:59.894 --> 00:44:02.289
- Can I have you autograph?
- No.

604
00:44:03.151 --> 00:44:05.685
And for Show and Tell, today,

605
00:44:05.710 --> 00:44:07.976
my big brother!

606
00:44:22.445 --> 00:44:24.456
Oh, I haven't seen you in a while.

607
00:44:24.481 --> 00:44:26.390
My whole life has changed, Linus.

608
00:44:26.422 --> 00:44:28.618
All of a sudden, everyone
wants to be my friend

609
00:44:28.643 --> 00:44:30.816
and yet,
I haven't really change.

610
00:44:30.841 --> 00:44:33.590
Do they like me for who I am?
Or for who they think I am?

611
00:44:33.615 --> 00:44:34.671
There he is!

612
00:44:34.696 --> 00:44:36.374
Charlie Brown, I need
you on my chess team.

613
00:44:36.399 --> 00:44:38.750
He's got no time for meaningless 
games, he's coming with me.

614
00:44:38.775 --> 00:44:39.829
- Close up!
- Huh?

615
00:44:39.854 --> 00:44:42.040
- His face.
- And action!

616
00:44:42.065 --> 00:44:43.939
Do you have time to help
me write my book report?

617
00:44:43.964 --> 00:44:45.249
It's due on Monday.

618
00:44:45.274 --> 00:44:47.619
Monday? 
The report is due on Monday?

619
00:44:47.644 --> 00:44:50.949
She's back on Monday!
I haven't even started yet!

620
00:44:50.974 --> 00:44:52.777
Does anyone know where Marcie is?

621
00:44:52.802 --> 00:44:55.166
She went skating with Peppermint Patty.

622
00:44:55.191 --> 00:44:57.322
Mr. Brown.
Mr. Brown!

623
00:44:57.347 --> 00:45:01.304
What about my exclusive?
Cut.

624
00:45:01.329 --> 00:45:03.402
There's Huckleberry Finn,

625
00:45:03.427 --> 00:45:05.196
The Catcher in the Rye.

626
00:45:05.221 --> 00:45:06.584
Sir,

627
00:45:06.609 --> 00:45:08.405
I've been sitting
here for hours,

628
00:45:08.430 --> 00:45:11.084
these are the greatest 
books of all time.

629
00:45:11.109 --> 00:45:12.896
- Please just pick one.
- Hmm.

630
00:45:12.921 --> 00:45:14.287
Let me sleep on it, Marcie.

631
00:45:14.312 --> 00:45:18.653
There's no time for sleeping, sir.
It's due Monday.

632
00:45:21.043 --> 00:45:25.700
Just my luck to get a partner that 
thinks Moby Dick was a hockey player.

633
00:45:25.725 --> 00:45:28.790
Marcie?
Where are you going?

634
00:45:30.077 --> 00:45:32.397
Hey!
Chuck, old boy.

635
00:45:32.422 --> 00:45:34.208
What brings you down here?

636
00:45:34.233 --> 00:45:36.314
I'm looking for Marcie.

637
00:45:38.722 --> 00:45:40.073
I need some advise.

638
00:45:40.098 --> 00:45:44.418
Curve ball not working for you?
Slap shot not strong enough?

639
00:45:44.443 --> 00:45:46.804
No.
I'm good with all that.

640
00:45:46.829 --> 00:45:50.829
I need to talk to Marcie about
finding the greatest book of all time.

641
00:45:50.854 --> 00:45:53.580
I just might be able to 
help you there, Chuck.

642
00:45:53.605 --> 00:45:57.144
Marcie just read off a 
long list of great novels.

643
00:45:57.169 --> 00:45:59.776
"Huckleberry Something, 
Catcher with a Pie."

644
00:45:59.801 --> 00:46:03.939
But she said the 
greatest book of all time

645
00:46:03.964 --> 00:46:06.357
is called "Leo's Toy Store"

646
00:46:06.382 --> 00:46:10.941
by some old guy 
called "Warren Peace".

647
00:46:10.966 --> 00:46:14.025
- "Leo's Toy Store"
- Yup! That's the one, Chuck!

648
00:46:14.051 --> 00:46:15.354
Thanks for the tip.

649
00:46:15.379 --> 00:46:17.680
Love that hustle, Chuck!

650
00:46:17.705 --> 00:46:20.388
[ LIBRARY ]

651
00:46:21.645 --> 00:46:24.936
Does anyone know where 
I can find "Leo's Toy Store"?

652
00:46:24.961 --> 00:46:26.715
- Shhh.
- Shhh.

653
00:46:27.790 --> 00:46:29.438
- Shhh.
- Shhh.

654
00:46:45.928 --> 00:46:47.036
Shhh.

655
00:46:47.061 --> 00:46:49.372
Leo's Toy Store.

656
00:46:49.397 --> 00:46:50.457
Nope.

657
00:46:50.482 --> 00:46:52.634
No. 
No.

658
00:46:52.738 --> 00:46:54.307
- Huh?
- No.

659
00:46:54.332 --> 00:46:56.482
Hm.
Where is it?

660
00:46:59.431 --> 00:47:01.842
He's going into 
the grown up section.

661
00:47:01.867 --> 00:47:03.875
Is that legal?

662
00:47:07.206 --> 00:47:08.429
Ahhh!

663
00:47:08.454 --> 00:47:09.584
Charles?

664
00:47:09.609 --> 00:47:11.375
I've never seen you
in here before.

665
00:47:11.400 --> 00:47:14.516
Oh, Marcie.
Thank goodness I found you.

666
00:47:14.541 --> 00:47:16.952
Can you help me find 
a copy of "Leo's Toy Store"?

667
00:47:16.977 --> 00:47:19.647
Did you say "Leo's Toy Store"?

668
00:47:19.672 --> 00:47:22.192
Yeah. Peppermint Patty told me
you said it was the greatest...

669
00:47:22.217 --> 00:47:25.739
Stop right there, Charles.
Come with me.

670
00:47:26.176 --> 00:47:28.849
This, is what you're looking for.

671
00:47:29.222 --> 00:47:32.013
LEO TOLSTOY's WAR and PEACE.

672
00:47:32.038 --> 00:47:33.680
Ohhh.

673
00:47:36.862 --> 00:47:39.557
Yikes.
How long was this war?

674
00:47:39.582 --> 00:47:42.222
Are you sure, that, is the 
book you want to read?

675
00:47:42.247 --> 00:47:43.884
Might I remind you, Charles.

676
00:47:43.909 --> 00:47:46.356
you only have the weekend
to complete your report.

677
00:47:46.381 --> 00:47:50.089
I have to, if I'm gonna 
win that gold star.

678
00:47:51.390 --> 00:47:52.720
Oh!

679
00:47:53.648 --> 00:47:55.499
I'm okay.

680
00:48:05.327 --> 00:48:06.670
Big book.

681
00:48:06.695 --> 00:48:09.876
How are you going to 
get it home, smarty pants?

682
00:48:18.523 --> 00:48:19.906
Huh, pretty smart.

683
00:48:19.931 --> 00:48:21.354
Huh! 
What am I saying?

684
00:48:21.379 --> 00:48:23.907
Good ol' Charlie Brown.

685
00:48:24.010 --> 00:48:26.452
Now, there's a guy 
who is going places.

686
00:48:26.477 --> 00:48:28.044
Whoaa!

687
00:48:39.078 --> 00:48:39.937
Thanks.

688
00:48:39.962 --> 00:48:41.625
AAUGH !

689
00:48:49.204 --> 00:48:51.173
- Huh?
- SURPRISE!

690
00:48:51.198 --> 00:48:52.747
Happy birthday.

691
00:48:52.772 --> 00:48:54.578
Who invited him?

692
00:48:58.312 --> 00:48:59.548
Huh?

693
00:49:11.054 --> 00:49:13.570
WAR and Peace.
Page 1.

694
00:49:13.594 --> 00:49:17.777
Eh bien, Mon prince, so Genoa...
(Well, Prince, so Genoa...)

695
00:49:20.463 --> 00:49:23.387
- Hey, Charlie Brow, come out and play!
- Hey, Charlie Brow, come out and play!

696
00:49:25.954 --> 00:49:27.505
- Sorry, guys.
- Ohh.

697
00:49:27.530 --> 00:49:28.980
Who reads a book on the weekend?

698
00:49:29.005 --> 00:49:30.599
Okay, where was I?

699
00:49:30.624 --> 00:49:34.213
... took a horse from a commander, 
and hungry and weary,

700
00:49:34.238 --> 00:49:37.710
... and the musketry fire 
sounded far away.

701
00:49:44.723 --> 00:49:48.004
... unimportance of life which 
no one could understand,

702
00:49:48.029 --> 00:49:50.447
... there was yesterday, 
and there was the day before.

703
00:49:50.472 --> 00:49:52.152
- Ooo.
- Ooo.

704
00:49:53.575 --> 00:49:54.667
- Aww.
- Aww.

705
00:49:54.692 --> 00:49:56.968
Okay, show's over!
Clear out!

706
00:49:56.993 --> 00:49:58.552
Will there be a late show?

707
00:49:58.577 --> 00:50:01.915
... and to recognize a 
dependence we do not feel.

708
00:50:01.940 --> 00:50:03.731
The end.

709
00:50:04.574 --> 00:50:06.161
I did it.

710
00:50:17.843 --> 00:50:20.445
It's all coming together now.

711
00:50:22.267 --> 00:50:28.471
Okay. This is my book report
about War and Peace.

712
00:50:28.496 --> 00:50:32.041
1, 2, 3, 4, 
5, 6, 7, 8, 9.

713
00:50:32.563 --> 00:50:36.460
First, there was war. 
Then there was peace.

714
00:50:36.485 --> 00:50:41.430
10, 11, 12, 13, 
14, 15, 16, 17 ?

715
00:50:42.223 --> 00:50:45.810
Only 983 words to go.

716
00:50:52.460 --> 00:50:53.917
Rats!

717
00:50:58.952 --> 00:51:00.827
This is no use.

718
00:51:00.852 --> 00:51:03.585
I'm just not as smart 
as they think I am.

719
00:51:03.610 --> 00:51:04.878
Huh!

720
00:51:10.703 --> 00:51:12.679
I can't let her down.

721
00:51:13.484 --> 00:51:16.688
There's still time.
You can do this.

722
00:51:17.111 --> 00:51:19.550
You can't give up
on her now.

723
00:51:26.719 --> 00:51:32.121
998, 999, 1000.
Finished!

724
00:51:40.626 --> 00:51:42.695
- Wake up, big brother!
- Augh!

725
00:51:42.720 --> 00:51:46.096
Today's the big assembly to
celebrate your perfect score!

726
00:51:46.121 --> 00:51:47.845
Come see!

727
00:51:48.839 --> 00:51:50.143
What are you up to *now*?

728
00:51:50.168 --> 00:51:53.684
Now that you're a big celebrity, 
we have to move fast.

729
00:51:53.709 --> 00:51:57.376
I have shirts, hats,
mugs and more!

730
00:51:57.401 --> 00:52:01.865
The fame that comes with intellectual 
superiority can be very fleeting.

731
00:52:01.890 --> 00:52:05.046
You have to cash in 
while you can.

732
00:52:05.135 --> 00:52:09.656
Today's going to be a big 
day for us, big brother.

733
00:52:14.211 --> 00:52:16.794
Thank you.
Come again soon.

734
00:52:17.204 --> 00:52:21.487
This is all for you, Charlie Brown.
You've really made it.

735
00:52:21.512 --> 00:52:22.852
It's going to happen.

736
00:52:22.877 --> 00:52:27.099
She's finally gonna notice me
for doing something great.

737
00:52:27.457 --> 00:52:29.337
Charlie Brown.

738
00:52:29.362 --> 00:52:31.885
I hate to admit it, you blockhead,

739
00:52:31.910 --> 00:52:37.032
but public opinion leads me to 
believe that after all these years,

740
00:52:37.057 --> 00:52:39.667
I *may* have been wrong about you.

741
00:52:39.692 --> 00:52:41.263
This is not easy for me!

742
00:52:41.288 --> 00:52:44.521
MY WHOLE WORLD HAS 
TURNED UPSIDE DOWN!

743
00:52:48.180 --> 00:52:51.866
Can I please have Charlie Brown 
come to the stage?

744
00:53:00.218 --> 00:53:02.729
It is my pleasure 
to present to you today,

745
00:53:02.754 --> 00:53:06.791
this award, for the highest achievement 
in this year's standardized testing.

746
00:53:06.816 --> 00:53:10.472
But before I do, 
the school proclamation.

747
00:53:11.001 --> 00:53:15.975
On this day whereas you have upheld 
the highest of academic standards,

748
00:53:16.000 --> 00:53:20.509
and whereas no one would have
ever expected that of you,

749
00:53:20.534 --> 00:53:25.272
and whereas you are the first
to ever receive a perfect score,

750
00:53:25.297 --> 00:53:29.843
therefore, be it resolved that today 
is declared Charlie Brown Day.

751
00:53:29.868 --> 00:53:32.397
Signed, Miss Othmar.

752
00:53:43.266 --> 00:53:45.385
That's my big brother.

753
00:53:48.620 --> 00:53:50.294
How about that, Charlie Brown.

754
00:53:50.319 --> 00:53:52.525
You're the star 
of the school now.

755
00:53:52.550 --> 00:53:54.657
Congratulations, Charles.

756
00:53:54.682 --> 00:53:57.949
Let me present you 
with your perfect test.

757
00:54:01.144 --> 00:54:02.834
☺
Oh, no.

758
00:54:02.859 --> 00:54:05.097
I must have signed 
the wrong paper

759
00:54:05.122 --> 00:54:06.672
Yeah!

760
00:54:19.199 --> 00:54:20.402
☺

761
00:54:25.579 --> 00:54:27.016
Before I begin,

762
00:54:27.041 --> 00:54:30.592
I'd like to thank all 
of you for your support.

763
00:54:32.816 --> 00:54:34.580
You have all been so kind.

764
00:54:34.605 --> 00:54:38.319
It is not often that I get 
this sort of recognition.

765
00:54:38.628 --> 00:54:40.954
But... um,

766
00:54:41.623 --> 00:54:43.685
there's been a mistake.

767
00:54:46.756 --> 00:54:49.748
This is not my test.

768
00:54:49.971 --> 00:54:52.409
HA! 
I knew it!

769
00:54:52.434 --> 00:54:53.667
Huh!

770
00:54:54.185 --> 00:54:55.927
Therefore,

771
00:54:56.778 --> 00:54:59.073
I cannot accept this honor.

772
00:54:59.098 --> 00:55:01.849
Can a brother and sister 
get a divorce?

773
00:55:01.874 --> 00:55:04.453
I think this belongs 
to Peppermint Patty.

774
00:55:04.478 --> 00:55:07.035
She's the real genius.

775
00:55:25.465 --> 00:55:29.434
That was a very admirable thing 
you just did, Charlie Brown.

776
00:55:30.150 --> 00:55:33.577
One moment I'm the hero, 
the next I'm the goat.

777
00:55:33.602 --> 00:55:37.746
Maybe things will go your way again,
after you hand in your book report.

778
00:55:38.017 --> 00:55:40.229
I'm not so sure.

779
00:55:40.458 --> 00:55:44.193
I was up all night working on it
and I can't remember a single word.

780
00:55:44.218 --> 00:55:47.200
Surely it's not as bad as 
you think, Charlie Brown.

781
00:55:47.225 --> 00:55:49.106
Let me see what you wrote.

782
00:55:52.614 --> 00:55:57.721
 Charlie Brown, the insight you bring to 
such a complex novel is beyond reproach!

783
00:55:57.746 --> 00:56:01.949
You two are sure to win the gold star 
with a book report of this quality.

784
00:56:01.974 --> 00:56:03.657
Book report?

785
00:56:03.682 --> 00:56:05.604
Were we supposed 
to do a book report?

786
00:56:05.629 --> 00:56:06.958
Oh, hi.

787
00:56:06.983 --> 00:56:09.003
In light of the fact 
that you were away,

788
00:56:09.028 --> 00:56:12.801
Charlie Brown took it upon himself to 
complete the report for the both of you.

789
00:56:12.826 --> 00:56:14.945
And I must say, this is 
one of the finest bits

790
00:56:14.970 --> 00:56:17.425
of literary analysis I've ever read.

791
00:56:17.450 --> 00:56:18.646
Ow!

792
00:56:28.708 --> 00:56:30.838
AAUGH !

793
00:56:32.795 --> 00:56:35.186
No. No. No.

794
00:56:40.303 --> 00:56:42.169
Good grief.

795
00:56:44.128 --> 00:56:46.326
Maybe we can fix it?

796
00:56:54.461 --> 00:56:55.821
Chapter 4

797
00:56:55.846 --> 00:56:57.862
Curse you, Red Baron!

798
00:57:36.014 --> 00:57:37.332
AHHH!

799
00:57:37.609 --> 00:57:38.762
- He did it!
- He did it!

800
00:57:38.788 --> 00:57:40.021
Oh.

801
00:57:58.566 --> 00:57:59.846
Aww.

802
00:57:59.871 --> 00:58:01.292
Blehh.

803
00:58:08.725 --> 00:58:10.049
Yikes!

804
00:59:16.853 --> 00:59:18.080
Yikes.

805
01:00:06.241 --> 01:00:11.735
The Flying Ace set out across 
the hostile countryside, undeterred.

806
01:00:44.013 --> 01:00:46.132
Whenever I feel really alone,

807
01:00:46.157 --> 01:00:49.341
I just sit and stare 
into the night sky.

808
01:00:49.366 --> 01:00:52.685
I've always thought that 
one of those stars was *my* star,

809
01:00:52.710 --> 01:00:54.581
 and at moments like this,

810
01:00:54.606 --> 01:00:57.810
I know that *my* star 
will always be there for me.

811
01:00:57.835 --> 01:01:02.025
Like a comfortable voice saying, 
"Don't give up, kid."

812
01:01:06.796 --> 01:01:09.579
The Flying Ace had to 
return to the aerodrome

813
01:01:09.613 --> 01:01:12.785
if he was ever 
to rescue Fifi.

814
01:01:35.427 --> 01:01:36.818
Hey!

815
01:02:16.678 --> 01:02:18.280
Shhh.

816
01:02:25.465 --> 01:02:30.148
♪ Christmas time is here ♪

817
01:02:30.173 --> 01:02:34.501
♪ Happiness and cheer ♪

818
01:02:40.550 --> 01:02:41.872
Yeah. 
Chuck?

819
01:02:41.897 --> 01:02:45.138
Your crazy dog is
over here again.

820
01:03:21.567 --> 01:03:22.825
Aww.

821
01:03:22.850 --> 01:03:24.898
Excuse me, mister.

822
01:03:24.923 --> 01:03:27.150
Have you ever flown a kite?

823
01:03:27.175 --> 01:03:29.602
Um.
Well... uh.

824
01:03:29.627 --> 01:03:32.097
Actually, let me just say that,

825
01:03:32.122 --> 01:03:34.718
I have years of experience 
with kites,

826
01:03:34.743 --> 01:03:36.071
- but I...
- That's great!

827
01:03:36.096 --> 01:03:38.942
Oh, uh, 
well, okay.

828
01:03:38.967 --> 01:03:42.348
The thing is, 
flying a kite isn't for everyone.

829
01:03:42.373 --> 01:03:44.411
It takes a certain type of person.

830
01:03:44.436 --> 01:03:46.447
It can be frustrating at times,

831
01:03:46.472 --> 01:03:48.233
they tend to have 
a mind of their own.

832
01:03:48.258 --> 01:03:51.905
But with determination and dedication,
you can make it happen.

833
01:03:51.930 --> 01:03:53.329
- Really!
- Here.

834
01:03:53.354 --> 01:03:56.163
You hold this string.
Plant your feet.

835
01:03:56.188 --> 01:04:00.672
Lean forward, knees bend,
back straight, head up

836
01:04:00.697 --> 01:04:03.448
and remember,
keep it simple.

837
01:04:03.721 --> 01:04:05.712
- Okay.
- Now, when I say go,

838
01:04:05.737 --> 01:04:07.438
run as fast as you can.

839
01:04:07.463 --> 01:04:09.682
Which way, mister?

840
01:04:13.466 --> 01:04:15.881
That way!
Now, go!

841
01:04:19.805 --> 01:04:22.672
I hope the little guy doesn't 
get discourage, Snoopy.

842
01:04:22.697 --> 01:04:25.196
He doesn't quite know 
how difficult this will be.

843
01:04:25.221 --> 01:04:28.182
It may take him years to 
gain my level of experience.

844
01:04:28.207 --> 01:04:30.205
It doesn't just happen over...

845
01:04:30.230 --> 01:04:30.824
Huh?

846
01:04:30.849 --> 01:04:33.491
Woo hoo!
It's flying!

847
01:04:33.516 --> 01:04:35.140
Wow!

848
01:04:35.165 --> 01:04:38.953
Thanks, mister.
You sure know your kites.

849
01:04:38.978 --> 01:04:41.109
Do you wanna try?

850
01:04:48.030 --> 01:04:51.283
You can do it!
Don't give up!

851
01:04:53.828 --> 01:04:55.163
Chapter 7

852
01:04:55.188 --> 01:04:57.157
Never give up!

853
01:04:58.810 --> 01:05:00.553
The Flying Ace 
knew this will be

854
01:05:00.578 --> 01:05:04.395
the last chance to save 
the love of his life.

855
01:08:32.608 --> 01:08:36.818
The Flying Ace returned to the 
aerodrome with the love of his life.

856
01:08:36.843 --> 01:08:39.545
He returned a hero.

857
01:08:45.786 --> 01:08:48.270
And so, as our hero observed

858
01:08:48.295 --> 01:08:52.330
he was destined to face the 
infamous Red Baron another day.

859
01:08:52.355 --> 01:08:54.038
A dog that flies?

860
01:08:54.063 --> 01:08:57.122
This is the dumbest thing 
I've ever read!

861
01:08:58.545 --> 01:08:59.810
Ow!

862
01:09:05.630 --> 01:09:09.130
AAUGH!
I got dog germs!

863
01:09:13.963 --> 01:09:16.132
- Come on, Charlie Brown!
- Come on, Charlie Brown!

864
01:09:16.157 --> 01:09:18.697
Hm.
Today calls for something special.

865
01:09:18.722 --> 01:09:20.197
Here we go.

866
01:09:21.588 --> 01:09:22.613
Hey, guys.

867
01:09:22.638 --> 01:09:24.859
It's the last day of school!

868
01:09:24.884 --> 01:09:27.147
Well, big brother, 
can you believe it?

869
01:09:27.172 --> 01:09:29.942
No more reading, 
writing, arithmetic!

870
01:09:29.967 --> 01:09:31.925
No more learning ever!

871
01:09:31.950 --> 01:09:33.167
What are you talking about?

872
01:09:33.192 --> 01:09:35.382
This is just the start
of summer vacation.

873
01:09:35.407 --> 01:09:37.607
You have eight more years 
of grammar school,

874
01:09:37.632 --> 01:09:39.112
four more years of high school,

875
01:09:39.137 --> 01:09:41.561
plus four more years of college.

876
01:09:41.602 --> 01:09:45.073
... four add the one to the extra four.

877
01:09:45.098 --> 01:09:48.215
It's over 37 years of school!

878
01:09:48.240 --> 01:09:51.853
I'll be bald and 
wrinkly by then!

879
01:09:55.123 --> 01:09:55.854
- Wow.
- Wow.

880
01:09:55.879 --> 01:09:57.310
Whoa!
Look at that!

881
01:09:57.335 --> 01:09:59.258
Is that Snoopy?

882
01:10:02.516 --> 01:10:03.994
Lucky.

883
01:10:04.441 --> 01:10:06.170
- Aww.
- Aww.

884
01:10:08.230 --> 01:10:10.195
Okay, everyone, listen up.

885
01:10:10.220 --> 01:10:12.577
I know this is the 
last day of school,

886
01:10:12.602 --> 01:10:14.054
- Yay!
- Yay!

887
01:10:14.079 --> 01:10:16.286
but, first, before we leave,

888
01:10:16.311 --> 01:10:18.026
we need to finish
picking our partners

889
01:10:18.051 --> 01:10:20.111
for this year's summer
pen pal project.

890
01:10:20.136 --> 01:10:20.929
- Aww!
- Aww!

891
01:10:20.954 --> 01:10:24.539
When I draw a name, stand 
if you want to be their partner.

892
01:10:24.564 --> 01:10:25.709
(Sigh)

893
01:10:25.823 --> 01:10:28.912
Here we go.
The next name is, Pig-Pen.

894
01:10:28.937 --> 01:10:32.573
I will. 
A little dirt never hurt anyone.

895
01:10:33.244 --> 01:10:35.586
- Schroeder!
- I do!

896
01:10:35.611 --> 01:10:38.228
Uh.
I mean, I will.

897
01:10:40.208 --> 01:10:41.885
Charlie Brown.

898
01:10:44.685 --> 01:10:46.919
- I will.
- Huh!

899
01:10:48.213 --> 01:10:49.908
She will?

900
01:10:50.569 --> 01:10:52.471
- Yay!
- Let's go.

901
01:11:01.674 --> 01:11:03.173
Hi!

902
01:11:05.460 --> 01:11:07.429
Charlie Brown,
where have you been?

903
01:11:07.454 --> 01:11:09.579
It's the first day of summer.

904
01:11:09.604 --> 01:11:12.364
You should be down there 
having fun with everyone else.

905
01:11:12.389 --> 01:11:14.963
I can't stop thinking about it, Linus.

906
01:11:14.988 --> 01:11:18.622
After all the humiliating disasters 
she witnessed this year,

907
01:11:18.649 --> 01:11:20.393
why would she choose me?

908
01:11:20.418 --> 01:11:22.406
Was she feeling sorry for me?

909
01:11:22.431 --> 01:11:26.158
 I don't want her to choose me just 
because she was feeling sorry for me.

910
01:11:26.183 --> 01:11:28.655
I have slightly more 
dignity than that.

911
01:11:28.680 --> 01:11:33.283
Charlie Brown, it might be time 
to consider the wild possibility

912
01:11:33.308 --> 01:11:37.065
that you're a good person
and that people like you.

913
01:11:37.090 --> 01:11:40.102
But you know, you'll never 
really know the answer unless...

914
01:11:40.127 --> 01:11:41.765
I just go up and talk to her.

915
01:11:41.790 --> 01:11:44.755
I should have listen
to you all along.

916
01:12:06.602 --> 01:12:08.179
Oh, Charles.

917
01:12:08.205 --> 01:12:10.401
I mean, Charlie Brown.

918
01:12:10.426 --> 01:12:12.310
She's not here?

919
01:12:12.335 --> 01:12:14.382
On her way to summer camp?

920
01:12:14.407 --> 01:12:16.516
So, the bus hasn't left school yet?

921
01:12:16.541 --> 01:12:18.631
But, it's about to leave?

922
01:12:20.501 --> 01:12:22.039
Oh, and by the way.

923
01:12:22.064 --> 01:12:24.302
It was a pleasure
to meet you, ma'am.

924
01:12:26.120 --> 01:12:27.986
- Charlie Brown!
- Charlie Brown!

925
01:12:28.336 --> 01:12:30.706
You blockhead!

926
01:12:31.904 --> 01:12:34.208
Woo!
All right!

927
01:12:49.605 --> 01:12:51.283
AUGH !

928
01:12:55.705 --> 01:12:57.151
Yay!

929
01:13:09.116 --> 01:13:10.951
AUGH !

930
01:13:19.653 --> 01:13:21.630
How do I get out of here?

931
01:13:31.241 --> 01:13:34.983
The whole world seems 
to be conspiring against me.

932
01:13:36.406 --> 01:13:41.035
I'm just asking for a little 
help for once in my life.

933
01:13:48.750 --> 01:13:51.188
Ugh.
Get out of here.

934
01:13:51.213 --> 01:13:52.704
Not you too!

935
01:13:52.729 --> 01:13:55.764
Whoa.
Whoooaaa!

936
01:13:55.789 --> 01:13:58.265
Hey, look, it's Charlie Brown!

937
01:14:04.117 --> 01:14:06.753
Charlie Brown is flying a kite?

938
01:14:06.778 --> 01:14:09.943
Charlie Brown is flying a kite!

939
01:14:12.295 --> 01:14:14.538
Wow!
Chuck's got a kite in the air.

940
01:14:14.563 --> 01:14:16.794
Way to go, Charles.
Whoa!

941
01:14:16.874 --> 01:14:18.816
- Huh?
- Huh?

942
01:14:18.841 --> 01:14:22.433
Charlie Brown is really doing it!
He's flying a kite!

943
01:14:44.248 --> 01:14:46.981
Oh, hi, Charlie Brown.

944
01:14:47.397 --> 01:14:49.413
You remembered my name?

945
01:14:49.438 --> 01:14:51.228
Of course I did.

946
01:14:51.827 --> 01:14:53.357
Before you leave,

947
01:14:53.382 --> 01:14:55.923
there's something 
I really need to know.

948
01:14:55.948 --> 01:14:59.585
Why, out of all the kids 
in our class,

949
01:14:59.756 --> 01:15:02.604
would you want to be 
partners with me?

950
01:15:03.103 --> 01:15:04.915
That's easy.

951
01:15:04.940 --> 01:15:08.072
 Because I've seen the 
type of person you are.

952
01:15:08.733 --> 01:15:12.155
An insecure, wishy-washy failure?

953
01:15:13.113 --> 01:15:15.496
That's not who you are at all.

954
01:15:15.521 --> 01:15:19.423
I like the compassion you showed 
for your sister at the talent show.

955
01:15:19.448 --> 01:15:21.915
The honesty you had
at the assembly.

956
01:15:21.940 --> 01:15:26.409
And at the dance, 
you were brave, and funny.

957
01:15:27.554 --> 01:15:29.350
And what you did for me,

958
01:15:29.375 --> 01:15:32.014
doing the book report 
while I was away,

959
01:15:32.039 --> 01:15:34.183
was so sweet of you.

960
01:15:35.445 --> 01:15:37.178
So, when I look at you,

961
01:15:37.203 --> 01:15:39.545
I don't see a failure at all.

962
01:15:39.570 --> 01:15:43.133
You have all the 
qualities that I admire.

963
01:15:43.840 --> 01:15:46.798
Sorry, I have to go now.

964
01:15:48.496 --> 01:15:49.824
Wait.

965
01:15:50.363 --> 01:15:52.750
I think this belongs to you.

966
01:15:52.775 --> 01:15:54.351
Oh, thank you!

967
01:15:54.376 --> 01:15:57.313
I've been looking
everywhere for this!

968
01:16:00.591 --> 01:16:02.943
 I'll write to you, pen pal.

969
01:16:04.578 --> 01:16:06.631
- Bye.
- Bye.

970
01:16:17.613 --> 01:16:19.666
Is he okay?

971
01:16:26.897 --> 01:16:31.212
It must feel pretty great being 
Charlie Brown right about now!

972
01:16:31.245 --> 01:16:32.720
You did it!

973
01:16:32.745 --> 01:16:34.091
Yeah!

974
01:16:34.200 --> 01:16:35.551
Nice job, Chuck!

975
01:16:35.576 --> 01:16:37.237
Good job, Charles.

976
01:16:37.262 --> 01:16:38.911
Hey, big brother!

977
01:16:41.822 --> 01:16:44.960
I'm proud to be 
your little sister.

978
01:16:45.819 --> 01:16:47.905
- Out of my way!
- Oh oh.

979
01:16:47.930 --> 01:16:51.496
I really need to tell you 
something, you blockhead!

980
01:16:51.528 --> 01:16:55.992
You're still full of surprises. 
Good ol' Charlie Brown.

981
01:16:56.017 --> 01:16:58.461
- YAY!
- YAY!

982
01:17:21.066 --> 01:17:26.181
Subtitle created by <font color="#ffff00">- Aorion -</font>

983
01:18:00.542 --> 01:18:02.620
Charlie Brown...

984
01:18:02.645 --> 01:18:06.986
Oh, Charlie Brown.
 I'll hold the football and you kick it.

985
01:18:07.011 --> 01:18:09.266
You *say* you'll hold it,
but what you really mean is

986
01:18:09.291 --> 01:18:12.678
you'll pull it away and I'll land  
on my back and I'll kill myself.

987
01:18:12.703 --> 01:18:15.129
But I feel I have really 
come to know you.

988
01:18:15.154 --> 01:18:17.526
I now understand that you are kind,

989
01:18:17.551 --> 01:18:20.067
compassionate, brave, and funny.

990
01:18:20.092 --> 01:18:24.507
No one would pull a football away from 
a person with all *those* qualities.

991
01:18:24.532 --> 01:18:26.786
She's right. 
I would never pull a ball

992
01:18:26.811 --> 01:18:29.562
away from someone 
with all *those* qualities.

993
01:18:29.587 --> 01:18:33.232
I am gonna kick this ball 
all the way to the moon.

994
01:18:36.430 --> 01:18:38.314
AAUGH!

995
01:18:39.295 --> 01:18:43.099
And gullible. 
I forgot to mention gullible.

996
01:19:34.715 --> 01:19:38.639
A round of root beers,
for our hero, The Flying Ace.

997
01:19:38.664 --> 01:19:40.268
- Yay!
- Yay!

998
01:19:45.251 --> 01:19:49.228
- Hip Hip.
- Hooray!

999
01:19:49.253 --> 01:19:50.439
Hip Hip.
